From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:53:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-ams968hh01: compensate ELVSS for the
 temperature

The vendor driver takes the ELVSS value of each luminance step, and the
ELVSS dim offset of each high brightness step, from three tables: above
0 C, above -20 C and below that. Its default is 20 C, and stock Android
writes the temperature into it from userspace. So far this driver used
the warm values only.

Take the panel temperature from an optional IIO channel ("temperature",
millidegrees Celsius), read at power-on and every 30 s while the panel
is on, and resend the brightness when the band changes. Without the
channel nothing changes.

The values are from the Samsung GPL kernel: device tree
dsi_panel_ANA38401_AMS968HH01_qxga_octa_cmd.dtsi
(samsung,smart_acl_elvss_tx_cmds_revA, _lowtemp_ and _lowtemp2_, mapped
to the steps by samsung,smart_acl_elvss_map_table_revA; the warm column
equals the values used so far) and driver
ss_dsi_panel_ANA38401_AMS968HH01.c (mdss_elvss(), mdss_hbm_etc(),
the 20 C default).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
